Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: draw nothing for an indexed draw without an index buffer

The runtime calls DrawIndexedPrimitive while no index buffer is set, for
example after SetIndices(NULL). The draw then failed the index size check
with E_INVALIDARG, and the application got E_FAIL where Windows expects
success. Return success without drawing, as there are no indices to
fetch.

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
@@ -3453,6 +3453,10 @@ D3D9DrawIndexedPrimitive(HANDLE hDevice,
       return E_INVALIDARG;
    if (!data->PrimitiveCount)
       return S_OK;
+   /* The runtime forwards an indexed draw made with no index buffer set.
+    * There are no indices to fetch: draw nothing and report success. */
+   if (!device->index_buffer && !device->index_sysmem)
+      return S_OK;
 
    return D3D9DrawDiffuse(device, data->PrimitiveType,
                           data->PrimitiveCount, 0, 0, true,
